§10 integrator at the fold. Cut by the chair's instruments lane from CTRL-TAPE's pass-4 PROPOSED
(schematic, not git-applyable — pass5/critique/CTRL-TAPE.md §3.4) and its pass-5 critic's rAF ladder.

The census scrolls ONE group per call and reads its tag at the scroll's own task and after each of
8 animation frames; the row asserts the SETTLED read (frame 8) and admits the publisher's lag
exactly — `lagFrames ≤ 2` (sync and rAF1 static, rAF2 sticky, both engines, both cells) — so it
forgives the mechanism's frame and nothing longer. The subject is named ONCE (`STICKY_SUBJECT`:
group, tag, head offset, floor), so CTRL-RULE's re-aim is a four-constant change
(`viewport-law-2.6-settle.on-RULE.diff` is that arm, applyable on 74a2b5d9 + CTRL-RULE). The
assertion, LEGIBLE (0.9) and the 40 px head are the row's own; nothing is re-worded to pass.

`git apply --check` exits 0 on 74a2b5d9 + each of CTRL-TAPE, ACC-GRAPHITE, ACC-FIVE, MOT-VERB and
FACE×VERB (the §2.6 block is byte-identical there); exit 1 on 74a2b5d9 + CTRL-RULE (RULE re-aims the
same census — use the on-RULE arm). Readings and negative controls: README.md §6.

